    {
      "id": "79b76a00-b565-41f1-b164-7eef9a5c913c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -576,
        -800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## 09-05-02 ai video clip pipeline with review and alerts\n\n### How it works\n- The channel RSS feed is watched and every new upload is read as a feed item.\n- Each video is checked against a Google Sheets log so it is only clipped once.\n- Reka Vision generates the clip, then the flow waits and polls the render status.\n- When the render is completed, the team gets a Telegram message and an email with the download link.\n- If the render is not finished after several checks, a failure alert is sent on both channels and the failed row is logged.\n\n### Setup\n- Replace the feed URL in Watch Channel Feed with your YouTube channel RSS feed URL.\n- Add your Reka API key credential to Create Clip in Reka and Fetch Render Status.\n- Create a Google Sheet with the columns video_id, title, clip_url, status, logged_at and set the CLIP_LOG_SHEET_URL environment variable.\n- Add Gmail and Telegram credentials, then set TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID to the chat you want alerts in.\n- Update the recipient address in Email Clip Link and Email Failure Alert.\n\n### Customization\n- Adjust the wait time and the retry limit to match how long clips take to render.\n- Toggle the subtitles option in Create Clip in Reka to switch captions on or off."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
